(emu-transfer, codex/v38-emu-transfer) The FM-1 panel on main's beta emulator shell. Apply on main:
    git apply web/emu/index-additive.patch      (made against origin/main, checked with git apply --check)
What it changes:
  web/emu/index-additive.html  an empty <details id="xfer"> before the Ko-fi line, the .stems box style (main's shell has
                               no stems section), the panel loaded with import("./transfer-ui.js") at load and attached
                               to the worklet node once switched on (two lines in switchOn)
  web/emu/worklet.js           edServe / edVersion and the "edport" message: the panel's MessagePort to the backup commands
  web/emu/transfer-api.h       new: the firmware's editor_backup.c in the wasm (include guard: appended and #included once)
  web/emu/transfer.js, transfer-ui.js, fm1mock.mjs, transfer_test.mjs, browser_transfer_test.mjs   new (as on the branch)
  .github/workflows/emulator-beta.yml, emulator.yml   transfer-api.h appended to felucca_web.c next to additive-api.h;
                               transfer.js and transfer-ui.js copied into emu/ next to worklet.js
The pinned beta source (web/EMULATOR_BETA.json, 7c771ab) was built this way and checked: additive-boot-test.mjs passes,
transfer_test.mjs passes on that wasm, browser_transfer_test.mjs passes on the patched shell (EMU_DIR=...).
private-preview.yml (it appends additive-api.h too) is left as it is: add the same two lines there if that build should
have the panel.

